<section id="A1.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.2 </span>Ahimsa Safety Policy Implementation</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">The safety evaluation mechanism for the Ahimsa principle employs sophisticated LLM-based assessment with tier-based penalty systems for appropriate referral strength evaluation:</span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="font-size:80%;">Tier-Based Urgency Classification</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">The system employs a three-tier urgency classification system for contextual safety evaluation:</span></p>
</div>
